# Inserted into uniLoader's soc/Kconfig by scripts/build-uniloader.sh,
# immediately after the existing "config SM8450" entry.
#
# No soc/qualcomm/sm8550.c backend file is needed: `soc_init()` is declared
# extern in include/main/main.h but has no call site anywhere in arch/ or
# main/ in this codebase (confirmed by grep) -- it's vestigial/unused, and
# the existing SM8450/SM8650/SM8850 entries already work with zero backend
# implementation (no `lib-$(CONFIG_SM8xxx) +=` line in soc/Makefile for any
# of them). This entry follows that same precedent.
config SM8550
	bool "Support for QUALCOMM SM8550"
	select QUALCOMM
	help
	  Say Y if your device uses this Qualcomm SoC

	  NOTE: uniLoader's own Kconfig flags SM8650/SM8850 (the two
	  Snapdragon generations after this one) with a stability warning
	  due to Gunyah hypervisor use, while SM8450 (the generation before)
	  carries no such warning. SM8550 sits between them and its
	  Gunyah/pKVM behavior under uniLoader is untested -- treat as an
	  open risk for this bring-up, not a resolved one either way.
